msgstr "Números pares e impares"

#. Help title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/ActivityInfo.qml:17
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Move the helicopter to catch the clouds having even or odd numbers."
msgstr "Move o helicóptero para coller as nubes que teñen números pares ou impares."

#. Help manual
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/ActivityInfo.qml:23
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Catch the clouds with an odd or even number, in the right order. With a keyboard, use the arrow keys to move the helicopter. With a pointing device, just click or tap on the target location. To know which number you have to catch you can either remember it or check the number on the bottom right corner."
msgstr "Colle as nubes de números pares ou impares na orde correcta. Co teclado, usa as teclas de frecha para mover o helicóptero. Cun dispositivo de punteiro, preme ou toca o lugar de destino. Para saber que número tes que coller, tes que lembralo ou comprobar o número na esquina inferior dereita."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:35
msgctxt "NumbersOddEven|"
msgid "This activity teaches about even and odd numbers."
msgstr "A actividade ensina os números pares e impares."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:39
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:49
msgctxt "NumbersOddEven|"
msgid "Even numbers are numbers which leave a remainder of 0 when divided by 2."
msgstr "Os números pares son os que teñen resto 0 ao dividilos entre 2."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:44
msgctxt "NumbersOddEven|"
msgid "What is meant by remainder?"
msgstr "Que é o resto?"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:53
msgctxt "NumbersOddEven|"
msgid "Odd numbers are numbers which do not leave a remainder of 0 when divided by 2."
msgstr "Os números impares son os que non teñen resto 0 ao dividilos entre 2."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:57
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:61
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/NumbersOddEven.qml:65
msgctxt "NumbersOddEven|"
msgid "Exercise to test your understanding."
msgstr "Practica para poñer a proba a túa comprensión."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/Tutorial1.qml:22
msgctxt "Tutorial1|"
msgid ""
"The remainder is the amount \"left over\" after dividing a number with another number.\n"
" If 6 is divided by 2 the result is 3 and the remainder is 0.\n"
" If 7 is divided by 2 the result is 3 and the remainder is 1."
msgstr ""
"O resto é a cantidade que «sobra» tras dividir un número entre outro.\n"
" Ao dividir 6 entre 2 o resultado é 3 e o resto é 0.\n"
" Ao dividir 7 entre 2 o resultado é 3 e o resto é 1."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/Tutorial2.qml:22
msgctxt "Tutorial2|"
msgid "For example: 12, 38, 52, 68, 102, 118, 168, 188, 502, 532, 700, 798, 842, 892, 1000. All of these numbers are even numbers as they leave a remainder of 0 when divided by 2."
msgstr "Por exemplo: 12, 38, 52, 68, 102, 118, 168, 188, 502, 532, 700, 798, 842, 892, 1000. Todos estes números son pares porque o resto é 0 ao dividilos entre 2."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/Tutorial3.qml:22
msgctxt "Tutorial3|"
msgid "For example: 15, 19, 51, 65, 103, 119, 169, 185, 505, 533, 701, 799, 845, 897, 1001. All of these numbers are odd numbers as they do not leave a remainder of 0 when divided by 2."
msgstr "Por exemplo: 15, 19, 51, 65, 103, 119, 169, 185, 505, 533, 701, 799, 845, 897, 1001. Todos estes números son impares porque o resto non é 0 ao dividilos entre 2."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:32
msgctxt "TutorialBase|"
msgid "Choose the even number:"
msgstr "Escolle o número impar:"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:32
msgctxt "TutorialBase|"
msgid "Choose the odd number:"
msgstr "Escolle o número par:"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:57
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:87
msgctxt "TutorialBase|"
msgid "Great"
msgstr "Xenial"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:61
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:91
#, qt-format
msgctxt "TutorialBase|"
msgid "There is an error: when divided by 2, %1 leaves a remainder of 1. Therefore this is an odd number."
msgstr "Hai un erro: ao dividilo entre 2, %1 ten resto 1. Polo tanto é un número impar."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:64
#: activities/numbers-odd-even/resource/TutorialBase.qml:94
#, qt-format
msgctxt "TutorialBase|"
msgid "There is an error: when divided by 2, %1 leaves a remainder of 0. Therefore this is an even number."
msgstr "Hai un erro: ao dividilo entre 2, %1 ten resto 0. Polo tanto é un número par."

