#. Activity title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:15
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Roman numerals"
msgstr "Números romanos"

#. Help goal
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:19
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Learn how to read roman numerals and do the conversion to and from arabic numerals."
msgstr "Aprende a ler números romanos e convérteos a números arábigos e ao revés."

#. Help manual
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:22
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Roman numerals are a numeral system that originated in ancient Rome and remained the usual way of writing numbers throughout Europe well into the Late Middle Ages. Numbers in this system are represented by combinations of letters from the Latin alphabet."
msgstr "Os números romanos son un sistema numérico orixinal da Antiga Roma e seguiu sendo a forma habitual de escribir números en Europa ata ben entrada a Baixa Idade Media. Neste sistema os números represéntanse mediante combinacións de letras do alfabeto latino."

#. +> trunk5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:23
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Learn the rules to read Roman numerals and practice converting numbers to and from arabic numerals. Click on the OK button to validate your answer."
msgstr "Aprende as regras para ler números romanos e practica a conversión de números co sistema numeral arábigo. Preme o botón de aceptar para validar a resposta."

#. +> stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:23
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Learn the rules to read Roman numerals and practice converting numbers to and from arabic numerals. Click on the OK button to validate your answer."
msgstr "Aprende as regras para ler números romanos e practica a conversión de números co sistema numeral arábigo. Preme o botón de aceptar para validar a resposta."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:25
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Digits: type arabic numerals"
msgstr "Díxitos: escribir números arábigos"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/ActivityInfo.qml:26
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Letters: type roman numerals (with I, V, X, L, C, D and M)"
msgstr "Letras: escribir números romanos (con I, V, X, L, V, D e M)"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:79
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:85
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid ""
"The roman numbers are all built out of these 7 numbers:\n"
"I and V (units, 1 and 5)\n"
"X and L (tens, 10 and 50)\n"
"C and D (hundreds, 100 and 500)\n"
" and M (1000).\n"
" An interesting observation here is that the roman numeric system lacks the number 0."
msgstr ""
"Os números romanos están formados por estes 7 números:\n"
"I e V (unidades, 1 e 5)\n"
"X e L (decenas, 10 e 50)\n"
"C e D (centos, 100 e 500)\n"
" e M (1000).\n"
" Curiosamente, no sistema de numeración romano non existe o 0."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:80
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:92
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:104
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:116
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:128
#, qt-format
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid "Convert the roman number %1 to arabic."
msgstr "Converte o número romano %1 en arábigo."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:86
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:98
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:110
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:122
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:134
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:140
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:146
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:152
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:158
#, qt-format
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid "Convert the arabic number %1 to roman."
msgstr "Converte o número arábico %1 en romano."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:91
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:97
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid ""
"All the units except 4 and 9 are built using sums of I and V:\n"
"I, II, III, V, VI, VII, VIII.\n"
" The 4 and the 9 units are built using differences:\n"
"IV (5 – 1) and IX (10 – 1)."
msgstr ""
"Todas as unidades excepto 4 e 9 fórmanse sumando I e V:\n"
"I, II, III, V, VI, VII, VIII.\n"
" 4 e 9 fórmanse usando restas:\n"
"IV (5 – 1) e IX (10 – 1)."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:103
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:109
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid ""
"All the tens except 40 and 90 are built using sums of X and L:\n"
"X, XX, XXX, L, LX, LXX, LXXX.\n"
"The 40 and the 90 tens are built using differences:\n"
"XL (10 taken from 50) and XC (10 taken from 100)."
msgstr ""
"Todas as decenas salvo 40 e 90 fórmanse sumando X e L:\n"
"X, XX, XXX, L, LX, LXX, LXXX.\n"
"40 e 90 fórmanse mediante restas:\n"
"XL (10 réstase a 50) e XC (10 réstase a 100)."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:115
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:121
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid ""
"All the hundreds except 400 and 900 are built using sums of C and D:\n"
"C, CC, CCC, D, DC, DCC, DCCC.\n"
"The 400 and the 900 hundreds are built using differences:\n"
"CD (100 taken from 500) and CM (100 taken from 1000)."
msgstr ""
"Todos os centos salvo 400 e 900 fórmanse mediante sumas de C e D:\n"
"C, CC, CCC, D, DC, DCC, DCCC.\n"
"400 e 900 fórmanse mediante restas:\n"
"CD (100 réstase a 500) e CM (100 réstase a 1000)."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:127
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:133
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid ""
"Sums of M are used for building thousands: M, MM, MMM.\n"
"Notice that you cannot join more than three identical symbols. The first implication of this rule is that you cannot use just sums for building all possible units, tens or hundreds, you must use differences too. On the other hand, it limits the maximum roman number to 3999 (MMMCMXCIX)."
msgstr ""
"As sumas de M úsanse para construír miles: M, MM, MMM.\n"
"Teña en conta que non pode unir máis de tres símbolos idénticos. O primeiro que implica esta regra é que non pode usar simplemente sumas para formar todas as unidades, decenas e centos posíbeis; tamén debe usar restas. Pola outra banda, limita o máximo número romano a (MMMCMXCIX)."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:139
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid "Now you know the rules, you can read and write numbers in roman numerals."
msgstr "Agora sabes as regras, podes ler e escribir números romanos."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:378
#, qt-format
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid "Roman value: %1"
msgstr "Valor romano: %1"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/roman_numerals/RomanNumerals.qml:379
#, qt-format
msgctxt "RomanNumerals|"
msgid "Arabic value: %1"
msgstr "Valor arábigo: %1"

