msgctxt "Data|"
msgid "Enter the weight of the gift in kilogram: %1"
msgstr "Insire o peso do agasallo en quilogramos: %1"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight/resource/5/Data.qml:13
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid "Balance up to 100 grams."
msgstr "Equilibrio ata 100 gramos."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight/resource/6/Data.qml:13
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid "Balance up to 10 kilograms including grams."
msgstr "Equilibrio ata 10 quilogramos incluíndo gramos."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight/resource/6/Data.qml:32
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid ""
"The \"kg\" symbol at the end of a number means kilogram. The kilogram is a unit of mass, a property which corresponds to the common perception of how \"heavy\" an object is. \n"
" Drop weights on the left side to balance the scales."
msgstr ""
"O símbolo «kg» ao final dun número significa «quilogramo». O quilogramo é unha unidade de masa, unha propiedade que se corresponde coa percepción común de como de «pesado» é un obxecto.\n"
"Solta pesos na esquerda para equilibrar as balanzas."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight/resource/6/Data.qml:44
#: activities/scalesboard_weight/resource/6/Data.qml:50
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid ""
"Remember, one kilogram (\"kg\") equals 1000 grams (\"g\"). \n"
" Drop weights on the left side to balance the scales."
msgstr ""
"Lembra que un quilogramo («kg») equivale a 1000 gramos («g»).\n"
"Solta pesos na esquerda para equilibrar as balanzas."

#. Activity title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/ActivityInfo.qml:15
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "Balance using the imperial system of units"
msgstr "Equilibra co sistema imperial de unidades"

#. Help manual
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/ActivityInfo.qml:23
msgctxt "ActivityInfo|"
msgid "To balance the scales, move some masses to the left or the right side (on higher levels). They can be arranged in any order. Take care of the weight and the unit of the masses, remember that a pound (lb) is 16 ounce (oz)."
msgstr "Para equilibrar a balanza move pesos á dereita ou á esquerda (en niveis superiores). Os pesos poden colocarse en calquera orde. Coida do peso e a unidade dos pesos, lembra que 1 libra (lb) son 16 onzas (oz)."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/1/Data.qml:13
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid "Balance up to 5 ounces."
msgstr "Equilibra ata 5 onzas."

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/1/Data.qml:18
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/2/Data.qml:18
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/3/Data.qml:18
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/5/Data.qml:18
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/6/Data.qml:18
#, qt-format
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid "%1 oz"
msgstr "%1 oz"

#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/1/Data.qml:26
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/2/Data.qml:26
#: activities/scalesboard_weight_avoirdupois/resource/3/Data.qml:26
msgctxt "Data|"
msgid ""
"The \"oz\" symbol at the end of a number means ounce. One pound equals sixteen ounces. \n"
" Drop weights on the left side to balance the scales."
msgstr ""
"O símbolo «oz» ao final dun número significa «onza». 1 libra equivale a 16 onzas.\n"
"Solta pesos na esquerda para equilibrar as balanzas."

